// Gobra contracts for the Logical clock — F7.
//
// These annotations are intended for verification with Gobra
// (https://github.com/viperproject/gobra). They compile away under standard
// `go build`. The discipline here is that Now() never decreases between
// successive calls without an intervening Tick().
//
// Gobra's mutex specs are stubs that prove data-race freedom under partial
// correctness only. Deadlock-freedom and starvation-freedom are out of scope.
//
// Stream 3 Phase 1a: introduce the LockP() permission predicate over the
// Logical clock. Conceptually: "the mutex `mu` is initialized and protects
// the `now` field." Callers can hold `acc(l.LockP())` as a permission
// token, and the constructors in clock.go fold this predicate after
// construction so it is available.
//
// Stream 3 Phase 1b: Now() and Tick() consume LockP() as a precondition,
// `unfold` it to access `l.now` under the lock, then `fold` it back as a
// postcondition. Both methods are no longer `// @ trusted` — the F7
// obligation (Tick advances by exactly 1; Now reads the current value) is
// now formally discharged by Gobra. The `sync.Mutex.Lock`/`Unlock` calls
// remain trusted via stubs/sync/sync.gobra (wrapper style — only the
// resource the mutex protects is reasoned about, not the mutex's own
// concurrency semantics).

package clock

// LockP is the lock-invariant predicate for *Logical. It abstracts the
// resource the mutex `mu` protects: write permission to `now`. Once Phase 1b
// drops the `// @ trusted` markers on Now()/Tick(), those methods will
// `unfold`/`fold` LockP() under the lock to access `now` legally.
//
// Body deliberately minimal: only `acc(&l.now)`. The mutex itself
// (`l.mu`) is a value-typed `sync.Mutex` field, and our `stubs/sync` declares
// no permission tokens on `Mutex` — so there is nothing to assert about
// `l.mu` here beyond the field-existence implied by `acc(l)` at the call
// sites. This keeps Phase 1a a pure additive setup with no stub surgery.
pred (l *Logical) LockP() {
	acc(&l.now)
}

// @ requires acc(l)
// @ ensures acc(l) && result == old(l.now)
// @ ensures l.now == old(l.now)
// @ pure
// @ func (l *Logical) GhostNow() (result int64)

// @ requires acc(l)
// @ ensures acc(l) && l.now == old(l.now) + 1
// @ func (l *Logical) GhostTick()
